1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
DarsLoop is a student workspace for Islamic classes. This explainer shows actual prepared fictional material.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The founder reports divided attention, missed lessons and difficult revision. These are observations, not a learner study.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Permitted sources become automatic notes. Students can choose note detail and study language before preparation.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Each supported explanation returns to an original audio time or genuine physical PDF page.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Choose Auto, Arabic, Urdu or English study material. Original quotations keep their source language.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Answer a lesson question, then review its supporting source. Quiz and flashcard progress stays private.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Mock exams use available prepared items. Written recall has a separate self-check, with no AI religious grading.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Catch-up, terms and study plans reuse source material. Personal rulings and hadith grading go to a qualified teacher.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
One hosted synthetic hour processed in 121.374 seconds after 55.112 seconds upload. This is one sequential English fixture.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Try the prepared fictional example and public code. Learning benefit, native quality and physical phone behavior still need evaluation.
